# The brave-search skill ships a vendored third-party Node tool: search.js,
# content.js and their npm manifests are MIT-licensed work by Mario Zechner, not
# Chapar code. Nothing in envs/, containers/, ci/, tools/ or validation/ executes
# them; they are agent tooling that happens to live in this repository.
#
# Marking them vendored keeps GitHub's language detection describing what this
# repository actually is.
#
# It does not fix the failing javascript-typescript code-scanning job, and was
